train-perf-flags.patch  (notes/hardware-spark.md, proposals P6 + P7; claims C118, C124; checks SQ74, SQ78)

Two independent, opt-in training flags (defaults keep every run bit-identical), plus launcher/campaign passthrough:
  --compile-mode M   torch.compile mode: default | max-autotune | max-autotune-no-cudagraphs | reduce-overhead.
                     Recorded in the run config ("compile_mode"). Adopt a non-default mode only if SQ74 shows
                     >= 8% at matched loss.
  --data-on-gpu      keep train.bin on the GPU as int32 (~1.05 GB of the 96 GiB carve-out) and gather batches
                     there. The CPU generator draws the same start indices, so batches are bit-identical to the
                     current path (SQ78 checks this); removes the per-step numpy gather, int64 cast,
                     pin_memory() and host->device copy (pinned memory is "limited" under WSL).
                     Recorded in the run config ("data_on_gpu").
Campaign lines may use both: E1 --seed 0 --compile-mode max-autotune-no-cudagraphs --data-on-gpu
Code paths: apply only as its own tagged version, and never while a campaign is queued (require-clean).
Apply: git apply notes/patches/train-perf-flags.patch

